{"id":"act-1","label":"Act 1","blocks":[{"k":"d","text":"A pavilion erected on the deck of a ship, richly hung with tapestry, quite closed in at back at first. A narrow hatchway at one side leads below into the cabin."},{"k":"h","level":3,"text":"Scene 1"},{"k":"d","text":"ISOLDA on a couch, her face buried in the cushions. —BRANGAENA holding open a curtain, looks over the side of the vessel."},{"k":"s","text":"THE VOICE OF A YOUNG SAILOR"},{"k":"d","text":"from above as if at the mast-head"},{"k":"v","lines":["Westward","surges slip,","eastward","speeds the ship.","The wind so wild","blows homeward now;","my Irish child,","where waitest thou?","Say, must our sails be weighted,","Filled by thy sighs unbated?","Waft us, wind strong and wild!","Woe, ah woe for my child!","O Irish maid!","my winsome, marvellous maid!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"starting up suddenly"},{"k":"v","lines":["What wight dares insult me?"]},{"k":"d","text":"She looks round in agitation."},{"k":"v","lines":["Brangaena, ho!","Say, where sail we?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"at the opening"},{"k":"v","lines":["Bluish stripes","are stretching along the west:","swiftly sails","the ship to shore;","if restful the sea by eve","we shall readily set foot on land."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["What land?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Cornwall’s verdant strand."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Never more!","To-day nor to-morrow!"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["What mean you, mistress? say!"]},{"k":"d","text":"She lets the curtain fall and hastens to ISOLDA."},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"with wild gaze"},{"k":"v","lines":["O fainthearted child,","false to thy fathers!","Ah, where, mother,","hast given thy might","that commands the wave and the tempest?","O subtle art","of sorcery,","for mere leech-craft followed too long!","Awake in me once more,","power of will!","Arise from thy hiding","within my breast!","Hark to my bidding,","fluttering breezes!","Arise and storm","in boisterous strife!","With furious rage","and hurricane’s hurdle","waken the sea","from slumbering calm;","rouse up the deep","to its devilish deeds!","Shew it the prey","which gladly I proffer!","Let it shatter this too daring ship","and enshrine in ocean each shred!","And woe to the lives!","Their wavering death-sighs","I leave to ye, winds, as your lot."]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"in extreme alarm and concern for ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Out, alas!","Ah, woe!","I’ve ever dreaded some ill!—","Isolda! mistress!","Heart of mine!","What secret dost thou hide?","Without a tear","thou’st quitted thy father and mother,","and scarce a word","of farewell to friends thou gavest;","leaving home thou stood’st,","how cold and still!","pale and speechless","on the way,","food rejecting,","reft of sleep,","stern and wretched,","wild, disturbed;","how it pains me","so to see thee!","Friends no more we seem,","being thus estranged.","Make me partner","in thy pain!","Tell me freely","all thy fears!","Lady, thou hearest,","sweetest and dearest;","if for true friend you take me,","your confidant O make me!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Air! air!","or my heart will choke!","Open! open there wide!"]},{"k":"d","text":"BRANGAENA hastily draws the centre curtains apart."},{"k":"h","level":3,"text":"Scene 2"},{"k":"d","text":"The whole length of the ship is now seen, down to the stern, with the sea and horizon beyond. Round the mainmast sailors are ensconced, busied with ropes; beyond them in the stern are groups of knights and attendants, also seated; a little apart stands TRISTAN folding his arms and thoughtfully gazing out to sea; at his feet KURVENAL reclines carelessly. From the mast-head above is once more heard the voice of the young sailor."},{"k":"s","text":"THE YOUNG SAILOR"},{"k":"d","text":"at the mast-head invisible"},{"k":"v","lines":["The wind so wild","blows homewards now;","my Irish child,","where waitest thou?","Say, must our sails be weighted,","filled by thy sighs unbated?","Waft us, wind strong and wild!","Woe, ah woe for my child!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"whose eyes have at once sought TRISTAN and fixed stonily on him—gloomily"},{"k":"v","lines":["Once beloved—","now removed—","brave and bright,","coward knight!—","Death-devoted head!","Death-devoted heart!—"]},{"k":"d","text":"laughing unnaturally"},{"k":"v","lines":["Think’st highly of yon minion?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"following her glance"},{"k":"v","lines":["Whom mean’st thou?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["There, that hero","who from mine eyes","averts his own:","in shrinking shame","my gaze he shuns—","Say, how hold you him?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Mean you Sir Tristan,","lady mine?","Extolled by ev’ry nation,","his happy country’s pride,","The hero of creation,—","whose fame so high and wide?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"jeeringly"},{"k":"v","lines":["In shrinking trepidation","his shame he seeks to hide,","While to the king, his relation,","he brings the corpse-like bride!—","Seems it so senseless","What I say?","Go ask himself,","our gracious host,","dare he approach my side?","No courteous heed","or loyal care","this hero t’wards","his lady turns;","but to meet her his heart is daunted,","this knight so highly vaunted!","Oh! he wots","well the cause!","To the traitor go,","bearing his lady’s will!","As my servant bound,","straightway should he approach."]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Shall I beseech him","to attend thee?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Nay, order him:","pray, understand it:—","I, Isolda","do command it!"]},{"k":"d","text":"At an imperious sign from ISOLDA BRANGAENA withdraws and timidly walks along the deck towards the stern, past the working sailors. ISOLDA, following her with fixed gaze, sinks back on the couch, where she remains seated during the following, her eyes still turned sternward."},{"k":"s","text":"KURVENAL"},{"k":"d","text":"observing Brangaena’s approach, plucks Tristan by the robe without rising."},{"k":"v","lines":["Beware, Tristan!","Message from Isolda!"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"d","text":"starting"},{"k":"v","lines":["What is’t?—Isolda?—"]},{"k":"d","text":"He quickly regains his composure as BRANGAENA approaches and curtsies to him."},{"k":"v","lines":["What would my lady?","I her liegeman,","fain will listen","while her loyal","woman tells her will."]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["My lord, Sir Tristan,","Dame Isolda","would have speech","with you at once."]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Is she with travel worn?","The end is near:","nay, ere the set of sun","sight we the land.","All that your mistress commands me,","trust me, I shall mind."]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["That you, Sir Tristan,","go to her,—","this is my lady’s wish."]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Where yonder verdant meadows","in distance dim are mounting,","waits my sov’reign","for his mate:","to lead her to his presence","I’ll wait upon the princess:","’tis an honor","all my own."]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["My lord, Sir Tristan,","list to me:","this one thing","my lady wills,","that thou at once attend her,","there where she waits for thee."]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["In any station","where I stand","I truly serve but her,","the pearl of womanhood.","If I unheeding","left the helm,","how might I pilot her ship","in surety to King Mark?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Tristan, my master,","why mock me thus?","Seemeth my saying","obscure to you?","list to my lady’s words:","thus, look you, she hath spoken:","“Go order him,","and understand it,","I—Isolda—","do command it.”"]},{"k":"s","text":"KURVENAL"},{"k":"d","text":"springing up"},{"k":"v","lines":["May I an answer make her?"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["What wouldst thou wish to reply?"]},{"k":"s","text":"KURVENAL"},{"k":"v","lines":["This should she say","to Dame Isold’:","“Though Cornwall’s crown","and England’s isle","for Ireland’s child he chose,","his own by choice","she may not be;","he brings the king his bride.","A hero-knight","Tristan is hight!","I’ve said, nor care to measure","your lady’s high displeasure.”"]},{"k":"d","text":"While TRISTAN seeks to stop him, and the offended BRANGAENA turns to depart, KURVENAL sings after her at the top of his voice, as she lingeringly withdraws."},{"k":"v","lines":["“Sir Morold toiled","o’er mighty wave","the Cornish tax to levy;","In desert isle","was dug his grave,","he died of wounds so heavy.","His head now hangs","in Irish lands,","Sole were-gild won","at English hands.","Bravo, our brave Tristan!","Let his tax take who can!”"]},{"k":"d","text":"KURVENAL, driven away by TRISTAN’S chidings, descends into the cabin. BRANGAENA returns in discomposure to ISOLDA, closing the curtains behind her, while all the men take up the chorus and are heard without."},{"k":"s","text":"KNIGHTS AND ATTENDANTS"},{"k":"v","lines":["“His head now hangs","in Irish lands,","sole were-gild won","at English hands.","Bravo, our brave Tristan!","Let his tax take who can!”"]},{"k":"h","level":3,"text":"Scene 3"},{"k":"d","text":"ISOLDA and BRANGAENA alone, the curtain being again completely closed. ISOLDA rises with a gesture of despair and wrath. BRANGAENA falls at her feet."},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Ah! an answer","so insulting!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"checking herself on the brink of a fearful outburst"},{"k":"v","lines":["How now? of Tristan?","I’d know if he denies me."]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Ah! question not!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Quick, say without fear!"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["With courteous phrase","he foiled my will."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["But when you bade him hither?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["When I had straightway","bid him come,","where’er he stood,","he said to me,","he truly served but thee,","the pearl of womanhood;","if he unheeded","left the helm","how could he pilot the ship","in surety to King Mark?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"bitterly"},{"k":"v","lines":["“How could he pilot the ship","in surety to King Mark!”","And wait on him with were-gild","from Ireland’s island won!"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["As I gave out the message","and in thy very words,","thus spoke his henchman Kurvenal—"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Heard I not ev’ry sentence?","it all has reached my ear.","If thou hast learnt my disgrace","now hear too whence it has grown.","How scoffingly","they sing about me!","Quickly could I requite them!","What of the boat","so bare and frail,","that floated by our shore?","What of the broken","stricken man,","feebly extended there?","Isolda’s art","he gladly owned;","with herbs, simples","and healing salves","the wounds from which he suffered","she nursed in skilful wise.","Though “Tantris”","The name that he took unto him,","as “Tristan”","anon Isolda knew him,","when in the sick man’s keen blade","she perceived a notch had been made,","wherein did fit","a splinter broken","in Morold’s head,","the mangled token","sent home in hatred rare:","this hand did find it there.","I heard a voice","from distance dim;","with the sword in hand","I came to him.","Full well I willed to slay him,","for Morold’s death to pay him.","But from his sick bed","he looked up","not at the sword,","not at my arm—","his eyes on mine were fastened,","and his feebleness","softened my heart:","the sword—dropped from my fingers.","Though Morold’s steel had maimed him","to health again I reclaimed him!","when he hath homeward wended","my emotion then might be ended."]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["O wondrous! Why could I not see this?","The guest I sometime","helped to nurse—?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["His praise briskly they sing now:—","“Bravo, our brave Tristan!”—","he was that distressful man.","A thousand protestations","of truth and love he prated.","Hear how a knight","fealty knows!—","When as Tantris","unforbidden he’d left me,","as Tristan","boldly back he came,","in stately ship","from which in pride","Ireland’s heiress","in marriage he asked","for Mark, the Cornish monarch,","his kinsman worn and old.","In Morold’s lifetime","dared any have dreamed","to offer us such an insult?","For the tax-paying","Cornish prince","to presume to court Ireland’s princess!","Ah, woe is me!","I it was","who for myself","did shape this shame!","with death-dealing sword","should I have stabbed him;","weakly it escaped me:—","now serfdom I have shaped me.","Curse him, the villain!","Curse on his head!","Vengeance! Death!","Death for me too!"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"throwing herself upon ISOLDA with impetuous tenderness"},{"k":"v","lines":["Isolda! lady!","loved one! fairest!","sweet perfection!","mistress rarest!","Hear me! come now,","sit thee here.—"]},{"k":"d","text":"Gradually draws ISOLDA to the couch."},{"k":"v","lines":["What a whim!","what causeless railing!","How came you so wrong-minded","and by mere fancy blinded?","Sir Tristan gives thee","Cornwall’s kingdom;","then, were he erst thy debtor,","how could he reward thee better?","His noble uncle","serves he so:","think too what a gift","on thee he’d bestow!","With honor unequalled","all he’s heir to","at thy feet he seeks to shower,","to make thee a queenly dower."]},{"k":"d","text":"ISOLDA turns away."},{"k":"v","lines":["If wife he’d make thee","unto King Mark","why wert thou in this wise complaining?","Is he not worth thy gaining?","Of royal race","and mild of mood,","who passes King Mark","in might and power?","If a noble knight","like Tristan serves him,","who would not but feel elated,","so fairly to be mated."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"gazing vacantly before her"},{"k":"v","lines":["Glorious knight!","And I must near him","loveless ever languish!","How can I support such anguish?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["What’s this, my lady?","loveless thou?"]},{"k":"d","text":"Approaching coaxingly and kissing ISOLDA."},{"k":"v","lines":["Where lives there a man","would not love thee?","Who could see Isolda","And not sink","at once into bondage blest?","And if e’en it could be","any were cold,","did any magic","draw him from thee,","I’d bring the false one","back to bondage,","And bind him in links of love.—"]},{"k":"d","text":"Secretly and confidentially, close to ISOLDA."},{"k":"v","lines":["Mindest thou not","thy mother’s arts?","Think you that she","who’d mastered those","would have sent me o’er the sea,","without assistance for thee?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"darkly"},{"k":"v","lines":["My mother’s rede","I mind aright,","and highly her magic","arts I hold:—","Vengeance they wreak for wrongs,","rest give to wounded spirits.—","Yon casket hither bear."]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["It holds a balm for thee.—"]},{"k":"d","text":"She brings forward a small golden coffer, opens it, and points to its contents."},{"k":"v","lines":["Thy mother placed inside it","her subtle magic potions.","There’s salve for sickness","or for wounds,","and antidotes","for deadly drugs.—"]},{"k":"d","text":"She takes a bottle."},{"k":"v","lines":["The helpfullest draught","I hold in here."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Not so, I know a better.","I make a mark","to know it again—","This draught ’tis I would drain."]},{"k":"d","text":"Seizes flask and shows it."},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"recoiling in horror"},{"k":"v","lines":["The draught of death!"]},{"k":"d","text":"ISOLDA has risen from the sofa and now hears with increasing dread the cries of the sailors."},{"k":"s","text":"VOICES OF THE CREW"},{"k":"d","text":"without"},{"k":"v","lines":["“Ho! heave ho! hey!","Reduce the sail!","The mainsail in!","Ho! heave ho! hey!”"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Our journey has been swift.","Woe is me! Near to the land!"]},{"k":"h","level":3,"text":"Scene 4"},{"k":"d","text":"KURVENAL boisterously enters through the curtains."},{"k":"s","text":"KURVENAL"},{"k":"v","lines":["Up, up, ye ladies!","Look alert!","Straight bestir you!","Loiter not,—here is the land!—","To dame Isolda","says the servant","of Tristan,","our hero true:—","Behold our flag is flying!","it waveth landwards aloft:","in Mark’s ancestral castle","may our approach be seen.","So, dame Isolda,","he prays to hasten,","for land straight to prepare her,","that thither he may bear her."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"who has at first cowered and shuddered on hearing the message, now speaks calmly and with dignity"},{"k":"v","lines":["My greeting take","unto your lord","and tell him what I say now:","Should he assist to land me","and to King Mark would he hand me,","unmeet and unseemly","were his act,","the while my pardon","was not won","for trespass black and base:","So bid him seek my grace."]},{"k":"d","text":"KURVENAL makes a gesture of defiance."},{"k":"v","lines":["Now mark me well,","This message take:—","Nought will I yet prepare me,","that he to land may bear me;","I will not by him be landed,","nor unto King Mark be handed","ere granting forgiveness","and forgetfulness,","which ’tis seemly","he should seek:—","for all his trespass base","I tender him my grace."]},{"k":"s","text":"KURVENAL"},{"k":"v","lines":["Be assured,","I’ll bear your words:","we’ll see what he will say!"]},{"k":"d","text":"He retires quickly."},{"k":"h","level":3,"text":"Scene 5"},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"hurries to BRANGAENA and embraces her vehemently"},{"k":"v","lines":["Now farewell, Brangaena!","Greet ev’ry one,","Greet my father and mother!"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["What now? what mean’st thou?","Wouldst thou flee?","And where must I then follow?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"checking herself suddenly"},{"k":"v","lines":["Here I remain:","heard you not?","Tristan will I await.—","I trust in thee","to aid in this:","prepare the true","cup of peace:","thou mindest how it is made."]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["What meanest thou?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"taking a bottle from the coffer"},{"k":"v","lines":["This it is!","From the flask go pour","this philtre out;","yon golden goblet ’twill fill."]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"filled with terror receiving the flask"},{"k":"v","lines":["Trust I my wits?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Wilt thou be true?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["The draught—for whom?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Him who betrayed!"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Tristan?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Truce he’ll drink with me."]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"throwing herself at ISOLDA’S feet"},{"k":"v","lines":["O horror! Pity thy handmaid!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Pity thou me,","false-hearted maid!","Mindest thou not","my mother’s arts?","Think you that she","who’d mastered those","would have sent thee o’er the sea","without assistance for me?","A salve for sickness","doth she offer","and antidotes","for deadly drugs:","for deepest grief","and woe supreme","gave she the draught of death.","Let Death now give her thanks!"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"scarcely able to control herself"},{"k":"v","lines":["O deepest grief!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Now, wilt thou obey?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["O woe supreme!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Wilt thou be true?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["The draught?"]},{"k":"s","text":"KURVENAL"},{"k":"d","text":"entering"},{"k":"v","lines":["Sir Tristan!"]},{"k":"d","text":"BRANGAENA rises, terrified and confused. ISOLDA strives with immense effort to control herself."},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"to Kurvenal"},{"k":"v","lines":["Sir Tristan may approach!"]},{"k":"h","level":3,"text":"Scene 6"},{"k":"d","text":"KURVENAL retires again. BRANGAENA, almost beside herself, turns up the stage. ISOLDA, mustering all her powers of resolution, walks slowly and with dignity towards the sofa, by the head of which she supports herself, turning her eyes firmly towards the entrance."},{"k":"d","text":"TRISTAN enters, and pauses respectfully at the entrance."},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Demand, lady,","what you will."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["While knowing not","what my demand is,","wert thou afraid","still to fulfil it,","fleeing my presence thus?"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Honor","Held me in awe."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Scant honor hast thou","shown unto me;","for, unabashed,","withheldest thou","obedience unto my call."]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Obedience ’twas","forbade me to come."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["But little I owe","thy lord, methinks,","if he allows","ill manners","unto his own promised bride."]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["In our land","it is the law","that he who fetches","home the bride","should stay afar from her."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["On what account?"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["’Tis the custom."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Being so careful,","my lord Tristan,","another custom","can you not learn?","Of enemies friends make:","for evil acts amends make."]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Who is my foe?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Find in thy fears!","Blood-guilt","gets between us."]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["That was absolved."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Not between us."]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["In open field,","’fore all the folk","our old feud was abandoned."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["’Twas not there","I held Tantris hid","when Tristan was laid low,","He stood there brawny,","bright and brave;","but in his truce","I took no part:","my tongue its silence had learnt.","When in chambered stillness","sick he lay","with the sword I stood","before him, stern;","silent—my lips,","motionless—my hand.","But that which my hand","and lips had once vowed,","I swore in stealth to adhere to:","lo! now my desire I’m near to."]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["What hast thou sworn?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"quickly"},{"k":"v","lines":["Vengeance for Morold!"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"d","text":"quietly"},{"k":"v","lines":["Mindst thou that?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"animated"},{"k":"v","lines":["Dare you to flout me?—","Was he not my betrothed,","that noble Irish knight?","For his sword a blessing I sought;","for me only he fought.","When he was murdered","no honor fell.","In that heartfelt misery","my vow was framed;","if no man remained to right it,","I, a maid, must needs requite it.—","Weak and maimed,","when might was mine,","why at thy death did I pause?","Thou shalt know the secret cause.—","Thy hurts I tended","that, when sickness ended,","thou shouldst fall by some man,","as Isolda’s revenge should plan.","But now attempt","thy fate to foretell me?","if their friendship all men do sell thee,","what foe can seek to fell thee?"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"d","text":"pale and gloomy, offers her his sword"},{"k":"v","lines":["If thou so lovedst this lord,","then lift once more my sword,","nor from thy purpose refrain;","let the weapon not fail again."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Put up thy sword","which once I swung,","when vengeful rancor","my bosom wrung,","when thy masterful eyes","did ask me straight","whether King Mark","might seek me for mate.","The sword harmless descended.—","Drink, let our strife be ended!"]},{"k":"d","text":"ISOLDA beckons BRANGAENA. She trembles and hesitates to obey. ISOLDA commands her with a more imperious gesture. BRANGAENA sets about preparing the drink."},{"k":"s","text":"VOICES OF THE CREW"},{"k":"d","text":"without"},{"k":"v","lines":["Ho! heave ho! hey!","Reduce the sail!","The foresail in!","Ho! heave ho! hey!"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"d","text":"starting from his gloomy brooding"},{"k":"v","lines":["Where are we?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Near to shore.","Tristan, is warfare ended?","Hast not a word to offer?"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"d","text":"darkly"},{"k":"v","lines":["Concealment’s mistress","makes me silent:","I know what she conceals,","conceal, too, more than she knows."]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Thy silence nought","but feigning I deem.","Friendship wilt thou still deny?"]},{"k":"d","text":"Renewed cries of the Sailors."},{"k":"d","text":"At an impatient sign from ISOLDA BRANGAENA hands her the filled cup."},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"advancing with the cup to TRISTAN, who gazes immovably into her eyes"},{"k":"v","lines":["Thou hear’st the cry?","The shore’s in sight:","we must ere long"]},{"k":"d","text":"with slight scorn"},{"k":"v","lines":["stand by King Mark together."]},{"k":"s","text":"SAILORS"},{"k":"d","text":"without"},{"k":"v","lines":["Haul the warp!","Anchor down!"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"d","text":"starting wildly"},{"k":"v","lines":["Down with the anchor!","Her stern to the stream!","The sails a-weather the mast!"]},{"k":"d","text":"He takes the cup from ISOLDA."},{"k":"v","lines":["I know the Queen","of Ireland well,","unquestioned are","her magic arts:","the balsam cured me","which she brought;","now bid me quaff the cup,","that I may quite recover.","Heed to my all-","atoning oath,","which in return I tender.—","Tristan’s honor—","highest truth!","Tristan’s anguish—","brave distress!","Traitor spirit,","dawn-illumined!","Endless trouble’s","only truce!","Oblivion’s kindly draught,","with rapture thou art quaff’d!"]},{"k":"d","text":"He lifts the cup and drinks."},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Betrayed e’en here?","I must halve it!—"]},{"k":"d","text":"She wrests the cup from his hand."},{"k":"v","lines":["Betrayer, I drink to thee!"]},{"k":"d","text":"She drinks, and then throws away the cup. Both, seized with shuddering, gaze with deepest emotion, but immovable demeanor, into one another’s eyes, in which the expression of defiance to death fades and melts into the glow of passion. Trembling seizes them, they convulsively clutch their hearts and pass their hands over their brows. Their glances again seek to meet, sink in confusion, and once more turn with growing longing upon one another."},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"with trembling voice"},{"k":"v","lines":["Tristan!"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"d","text":"overpowered"},{"k":"v","lines":["Isolda!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"sinking upon his breast"},{"k":"v","lines":["Traitor beloved!"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Woman divine!"]},{"k":"d","text":"He embraces her with ardor. They remain in a silent embrace."},{"k":"s","text":"ALL THE MEN"},{"k":"d","text":"without"},{"k":"v","lines":["Hail! Hail!","Hail our monarch!","Hail to Mark, the king!"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"who, filled with confusion and horror, has leaned over the side with averted face, now turns to behold the pair locked in their close embrace, and rushes to the front, wringing her hands in despair"},{"k":"v","lines":["Woe’s me! Woe’s me!","Endless mis’ry","I have wrought","instead of death!","Dire the deed","of my dull fond heart:","it cries aloud to heav’n!"]},{"k":"d","text":"They start from their embrace."},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"d","text":"bewildered"},{"k":"v","lines":["What troubled dream","of Tristan’s honor?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["What troubled dream","Of Isolda’s shame?"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Have I then lost thee?"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Have I repulsed thee?"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Fraudulent magic,","framing deceit!"]},{"k":"s","text":"BOTH"},{"k":"v","lines":["Languishing passion,","longing and growing,","love ever yearning,","loftiest glowing!","Rapture confess’d","rides in each breast!","Isolda! Tristan!","Tristan! Isolda!","World, I can shun thee","my love is won me!","Thou’rt my thought, all above:","highest delight of love!"]},{"k":"h","level":3,"text":"Scene 7"},{"k":"d","text":"The curtains are now drawn wide apart; the whole ship is covered with knights and sailors, who, with shouts of joy, make signs over towards the shore which is now seen to be quite near, with castle-crowned cliffs. Tristan and Isolda remain absorbed in mutual contemplation, perceiving nothing that is passing."},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"to the women, who at her bidding ascend from below"},{"k":"v","lines":["Quick—the mantle!","the royal robe!—"]},{"k":"d","text":"Rushing between TRISTAN and ISOLDA."},{"k":"v","lines":["Up, hapless ones!","See where we are!"]},{"k":"d","text":"She places the royal mantle on ISOLDA, who notices nothing."},{"k":"s","text":"ALL THE MEN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Hail! Hail!","Hail our monarch!","Hail to Mark the king!"]},{"k":"s","text":"KURVENAL"},{"k":"d","text":"advancing gaily"},{"k":"v","lines":["Hail, Tristan,","knight of good hap!","Behold King Mark approaching,","in a bark","with brave attendance.","Gladly he stems the tide,","coming to seek his bride."]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"d","text":"looking up in bewilderment"},{"k":"v","lines":["Who comes?"]},{"k":"s","text":"KURVENAL"},{"k":"v","lines":["The king ’tis."]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["What king mean you?"]},{"k":"d","text":"KURVENAL points over the side. TRISTAN gazes stupefied at the shore."},{"k":"s","text":"ALL THE MEN"},{"k":"d","text":"waving their hats"},{"k":"v","lines":["Hail to King Mark! All hail!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"bewildered"},{"k":"v","lines":["What is’t, Brangaena?","What are those cries?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Isolda—mistress!","Compose thyself!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Where am I! living?","What was that draught?"]},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"despairingly"},{"k":"v","lines":["The love-potion!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"d","text":"staring with horror at TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Tristan!"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["Isolda!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ISOLDA"},{"k":"v","lines":["Must I live, then?"]},{"k":"d","text":"Falls fainting upon his breast."},{"k":"s","text":"BRANGAENA"},{"k":"d","text":"to the women"},{"k":"v","lines":["Look to your lady!"]},{"k":"s","text":"TRISTAN"},{"k":"v","lines":["O rapture fraught with cunning!","O fraud with bliss o’er-running!"]},{"k":"s","text":"ALL THE MEN"},{"k":"d","text":"in a general burst of acclamation"},{"k":"v","lines":["Hail to King Mark!","Cornwall, hail!"]},{"k":"d","text":"People have clambered over the ship’s side, others have extended a bridge, and the aspect of all indicates the immediate arrival of the expected ones, as the curtain falls."}]}